  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri. Mallikarjuna T V vs Smt. N Radha on 18 January, 2024 Author: Pradeep Singh Yerur Bench: Pradeep Singh Yerur -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:2381 Mfa No. 3042 of 2021 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 18Th Day Of January, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr Justice Pradeep Singh Yerur Miscellaneous First Appeal No. 3042 Of 2021 (Mv-I) Between: Sri. Mallikarjuna T V S/O T.Y. Venkatsh @ Venkateshappa, Now Aged About 23 Years, Residing At Thoti Village And Post, Kolar Taluk And District. ...Appellant (By Sri. Gopal Krishna N., Advocate) And: 1. Smt. N. Radha W/O Late M. Shivanna, Now Aged About 55 Years, Residing At Vinobha Volony, Chinthamani Taluk, Chikkaballapura District-563125. Digitally signed by B 2. M/S United India Insurance Company Ltd., Lavanya Regional Office, 5Th Floor, Location: Krushi Bhavana, High Nrupathunga Road, Court Of Karnataka Hudson Circle, Bengaluru-560001 By Its Manager. ...Respondents (By Sri. K. Nagarajaiah, Advocate For R-2; Notice To R-1 Is Dispensed With) Sri. Mallikarjuna T V vs Smt. N Radha on 18 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/187647009/ 1 This Mfa Is Filed U/S 173(1) Of Mv Act, 1988 Against The Judgment And Award Dated 14.10.2019 -2- Nc: 2024:Khc:2381 Mfa No. 3042 of 2021 Passed In Mvc No.7126/2017 On The File Of The Member, Mact, Xviii Additional Judge, Court Of Small Causes, Bengaluru Scch-4, Partly Allowing The Claim Petition For Compensation And Seeking Enhancement Of Compensation. This Appeal, Coming On For Admission, This Day, The Court Delivered The Following: Judgment",
    "facts": "Due to the impact of the vehicle the claimant fell down and sustained grievous injuries to his head and other parts of the body. The claimant was shifted to R.L.Jalappa Hospital, Kolar, wherein he took treatment as first aid and thereafter shifted to Pulse Hospital, Bengaluru. The claimant was examined and found to be defuse axonal injury and with multiple fracture. He was treated as inpatient and discharged on 08.04.2017. He was subsequently admitted again on 10.04.2017 at SNR Government Hospital, Kolar and again he was inpatient till 18.05.2017. Sri . Mallikarjuna T V vs Smt. N Radha on 18 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/187647009/ 2 NC: 2024:KHC:2381 p.m., as a Caterer. Due to occurrence of the accident, the injuries sustained permanent disability, unable to do his work as he was prior to occurrence of accident. On the basis of complaint, a criminal case is registered against the driver of the Tractor and Trailer for the offence punishable under Sections 279 and 337 of IPC. Hence, the claim petition came to be filed by the claimant. Respondent No.2 filed detail statement of objections denying the allegations made in the claim petition including the issuance of policy to the offending vehicle and the negligence attributed to the driver of the offending vehicle, also denied the age, avocation and income stated by the claimant and sought for dismissal of the claim petition.",
    "arguments": "It has awarded just and reasonable compensation on the basis of material placed on record. Admittedly, there is no proof of income placed by the claimant. Hence, tribunal has rightly assessed the income to be Rs.10,000/- p.m which does not call for interference. He also contends that on other heads the Tribunal awarded suitable compensation which also does not call for interference."
  },
